# Python Code Conventions

## Import Organization
- Standard library imports first
- Third-party imports second  
- Local imports last
- Use `sys.path.append()` for local module imports when needed

## Path Handling
- Always use absolute paths for data and model files
- Use `os.path.join()` for cross-platform path construction
- Reference paths relative to project root: `/media/erc/GPU/projects/aagha-ii/intent_aware_layout_generation/`

## PyTorch Conventions
- Use `torch.device()` for device management
- Set `CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1` for debugging
- Use `torch.cuda.set_device()` for multi-GPU setups
- Always specify `map_location` when loading checkpoints

## Configuration Management
- Use YAML configs in [code/configs/](mdc:code/configs/)
- Load configs with `load_config()` utility function
- Override config values with command line arguments

## Error Handling
- Use try-except blocks for file operations
- Log errors with the project logger
- Provide meaningful error messages